.git
.venv
.env
.env.*
backend/db.sqlite3
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
build
logs
downloaded_cases
media
# Roughly 780MB of case law, treatises, templates and letterheads. None of it
# belongs in the image: production reads this content from the Azure Files
# shares mounted at /app/storage, and the deploy script uploads it there
# directly from the checkout. Baking it in would put three quarters of a
# gigabyte on the wire for every cold-start image pull to no purpose.
#
# It is a private submodule, so CI never had it and CI images were always lean.
# This line is what keeps an image built from a developer's machine -- which
# does have it checked out -- the same size as the one CI builds.
private-content
**/__pycache__
*.pyc

# Nothing the running container reads. Every megabyte here is pulled and
# unpacked on a cold start, which is measurably a function of image size.
docs
brainstorming
clickable_prototype.js
.agents
.codex
.claude
.github
